        {
          "title": "The GIL and Concurrency Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What the GIL Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==GIL== = a mutex in CPython",
                "Only **one thread** runs Python bytecode at a time",
                "True even on a ==multi-core== machine",
                "It guards interpreter internals, e.g. {blue:reference counts}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Not atomic",
              "text": "The GIL does not make compound operations safe. `count += 1` is read, add, write, so it still needs a ==Lock==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. When Threads Overlap",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "GIL is ==released== during blocking I/O: sockets, files, `sleep`",
                "Also released in many C extensions: ==NumPy==, `hashlib`",
                "Pure Python number crunching holds the GIL: {red:no overlap}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Concurrency",
                "Parallelism"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Meaning",
                  "Tasks **interleave**",
                  "Code runs at the **same instant**"
                ],
                [
                  "Tools",
                  "threads, `asyncio`",
                  "==processes==; threads only in GIL-releasing C or free-threaded builds"
                ],
                [
                  "Python code on many cores",
                  "No",
                  "Yes"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Decision Rule",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flowchart",
              "spec": {
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "q"
                  ],
                  [
                    "io",
                    "cpu"
                  ]
                ],
                "nodes": {
                  "q": {
                    "text": "What is the work waiting on?",
                    "shape": "diamond"
                  },
                  "io": {
                    "text": "Network / disk (I/O-bound): threads or asyncio",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  "cpu": {
                    "text": "Number crunching (CPU-bound): processes",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                },
                "edges": [
                  {
                    "from": "q",
                    "to": "io",
                    "label": "waiting"
                  },
                  {
                    "from": "q",
                    "to": "cpu",
                    "label": "computing"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Remember",
              "items": [
                "Threads help ==waiting==, not computing",
                "Processes each have their own GIL",
                "Shared counter in threads: use a Lock"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Threading for I/O-Bound Work",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Threading for I/O-Bound Work",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Threads and Locks",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Thread(target=fn, args=(x,))`, then `t.start()`",
                "`t.join()` ==blocks== until the thread finishes",
                "Threads **share memory**: guard shared state with `with lock:`",
                "No lock means a ==race condition==, e.g. on `n += 1`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import threading",
                "n, lock = 0, threading.Lock()",
                "def bump():",
                "    global n",
                "    with lock: n += 1",
                "t = threading.Thread(target=bump); t.start(); t.join()",
                "print(n)"
              ],
              "note": "Lock guards the shared counter"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "1"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Daemon, Queue, CPU",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "`daemon`",
                "When main exits"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`True`",
                  "{red:killed abruptly}"
                ],
                [
                  "`False` (default)",
                  "{green:keeps program alive}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`queue.Queue` is the thread-safe producer to consumer handoff",
                "`put()` adds, `get()` blocks, `task_done()` marks the job done"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import queue, threading",
                "q = queue.Queue()",
                "def worker():  # consumer thread",
                "    print(q.get()); q.task_done()",
                "threading.Thread(target=worker, daemon=True).start()",
                "q.put(\"job\")  # producer: main thread",
                "q.join()"
              ],
              "note": "join() waits until every task_done()"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "job"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "CPU-bound code",
              "text": "Threads give ==no speedup== under the GIL, and lock contention plus switching can make them **slower**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Multiprocessing for CPU-Bound Work",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Multiprocessing for CPU-Bound Work",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Separate Processes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each `Process` has its ==own interpreter== and ==own GIL==",
                "CPU-bound work runs in {green:true parallel} across cores",
                "No shared memory, and ==startup cost== is higher than threads"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Guard and Pool",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Guard the entry point with ==`if __name__ == '__main__':`==",
                "Spawn (Windows, macOS): child **re-imports** the module, reaches the start call and dies with `RuntimeError`",
                "`Pool(n).map(fn, items)` splits work across n workers",
                "`with Pool() as p:` cleans up; ==chunksize== batches many small tasks"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from multiprocessing import Pool",
                "",
                "if __name__ == '__main__':",
                "    with Pool(4) as p:",
                "        out = p.map(fn, items, chunksize=100)"
              ],
              "note": "fn must be a top-level function"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Data Between Processes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Pickle args",
                    "sub": "parent",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Unpickle",
                    "sub": "worker",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Run fn",
                    "sub": "own GIL",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Pickle result",
                    "sub": "back to parent",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lambdas, open files, sockets cannot be pickled",
                "Large objects are costly to copy both ways"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Use for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Queue`",
                  "many producers and consumers"
                ],
                [
                  "`Pipe`",
                  "two endpoints"
                ],
                [
                  "`shared_memory`",
                  "big buffers, no copy"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Missing guard",
              "text": "Without the ==`__main__` guard==, spawn re-runs top-level code in every child, which stops with `RuntimeError`, so **no work** gets done."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "concurrent.futures Executors",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "concurrent.futures Executors",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. One Interface, Two Pools",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Both pools share ==one interface==: `submit`, `map`, `shutdown`",
                "Switching is a ==one-word change==: swap the class name"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pool",
                "Workload"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`ThreadPoolExecutor`",
                  "{green:I/O-bound}"
                ],
                [
                  "`ProcessPoolExecutor`",
                  "{orange:CPU-bound}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Getting Results",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Gives",
                "Order",
                "Error raised"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`submit(fn, *args)`",
                  "`Future`",
                  "you choose",
                  "at `result()`"
                ],
                [
                  "`map(fn, items)`",
                  "results",
                  "input order",
                  "first one, while iterating"
                ],
                [
                  "`as_completed(fs)`",
                  "futures",
                  "finish order",
                  "at `result()`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`future.result(timeout=)` blocks and ==re-raises== worker errors",
                "`as_completed`: progress, handle fast results first",
                "`wait()` blocks until ==all== or ==first== complete"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "with ThreadPoolExecutor() as ex:",
                "    futs = [ex.submit(fn, u) for u in urls]",
                "    for f in as_completed(futs):",
                "        data = f.result(timeout=5)",
                "    ordered = list(ex.map(fn, urls))"
              ],
              "note": "swap in ProcessPoolExecutor for CPU work"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Never calling `.result()`: the exception is ==silently swallowed==",
                "Skipping `with` and `shutdown()`: workers linger until exit"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Always use with",
              "text": "Leaving the `with` block shuts the pool down and ==joins== the workers."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "asyncio Basics and Free-Threaded Python 3.13+",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "asyncio Basics and Free-Threaded Python 3.13+",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Coroutines and Awaiting",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Calling `async def` only makes a ==coroutine object==; it runs when awaited or scheduled",
                "Entry point: `asyncio.run(main())`",
                "`await` {blue:yields to the event loop}; one thread runs many tasks ==cooperatively==",
                "One blocking call (`time.sleep`, `requests.get`) {red:freezes every task}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Running Tasks Together",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Behaviour"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`create_task(coro())`",
                  "schedules it to run concurrently"
                ],
                [
                  "`await gather(a(), b())`",
                  "runs together, results in ==call order=="
                ],
                [
                  "`asyncio.TaskGroup` (3.11+)",
                  "structured errors via `ExceptionGroup`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import asyncio",
                "async def job(n):",
                "    await asyncio.sleep(0.1)",
                "    return n * 2",
                "async def main():",
                "    print(await asyncio.gather(job(1), job(2)))",
                "    print(await asyncio.to_thread(len, 'abc'))",
                "asyncio.run(main())"
              ],
              "note": "gather and to_thread"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "[2, 4]",
                "3"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Blocking Calls and Free-Threading",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Use `await asyncio.sleep()`, never `time.sleep()`",
                "Unavoidable blocking call: `await asyncio.to_thread(fn)`",
                "==Free-threaded== build (PEP 703, `python3.13t`) removes the GIL; threads run Python in parallel",
                "{orange:Experimental} in 3.13: some single-thread slowdown, extensions must be compatible"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No GIL is not no locks",
              "text": "Shared mutable state still needs a `Lock`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Choosing and Using Concurrency Tools",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Choosing and Using Concurrency Tools",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Picker",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Workload",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Network or disk waiting, modest scale",
                  "`ThreadPoolExecutor`"
                ],
                [
                  "Thousands of connections, async libraries",
                  "`asyncio`"
                ],
                [
                  "CPU-heavy",
                  "`ProcessPoolExecutor` or `Pool`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Core calls",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Call"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Thread",
                  "`Thread(target=fn, args=(x,)).start()`, `join()`"
                ],
                [
                  "Pool",
                  "`Pool(n).map(fn, items)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Executor",
                  "`executor.submit(fn, x)`, `executor.map(fn, items)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Finish order",
                  "`as_completed(futures)`"
                ],
                [
                  "asyncio",
                  "`asyncio.run(main())`"
                ],
                [
                  "Run together",
                  "`await asyncio.gather(a(), b())`"
                ],
                [
                  "Blocking call",
                  "`await asyncio.to_thread(fn)`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common errors",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Missing ==`__main__` guard== in multiprocessing",
                "==Unpicklable== arguments: lambdas, files, sockets",
                "Blocking call inside `async def`",
                "==Un-awaited== coroutine never runs",
                "Shared counter without a `Lock`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Free-threaded check and rule",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "python -c \"import sys; print(sys._is_gil_enabled())\"  # 3.13+",
                "python3.13t app.py  # free-threaded build",
                "PYTHON_GIL=0 python3.13t app.py  # force GIL off"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule of thumb",
              "text": "==Measure first.== Threads for I/O, processes for CPU, asyncio for thousands of connections. Free-threaded only after library support is confirmed."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
